title: Leuchtenberg takes power.
subtitle: The beginning of the end.
view-if: chancellor == "Leuchtenberg" or president == "Leuchtenberg" or chancellor_party == "NTS"
on-arrival: rsdrp_in_government = 0
tags: event
new-page: true

[? if leuchtenberg_deported and president != "Leuchtenberg" and chancellor != "Leuchtenberg": The first act that Chancellor [+ chancellor +] takes upon assuming office is bringing Sergey Leuchtenberg back to Russia, and giving him citizenship and an official cabinet position. ?]

Leuchtenberg has promised a campaign of revenge against the socialists, and the Solidarists have already spilled much blood on the streets. In his published manifesto, he promises a campaign of unspeakable horror against our Jews, and endless wars of violent expansion that will ruin all of Europe.

What are we to do now?

- @fight: We will fight on the streets to prevent Leuchtenberg from taking power.
- @give_up: We will vote against the Solidarists in the Reichstag.


@fight

Do we realize that this means civil war, against the full force of the state?

- @civil_war: Yes.
- @give_up: We are not ready for war. Instead, we will vote against the Solidarists in the Reichstag.

@give_up

Speeches are made. Votes are held. Bullets fly in the streets. Some socialists are killed or jailed. Others flee the country. What can votes even do at this juncture?

The Reichstag is burned, ostensibly by a foreign communist. In the wake, the Solidarists pass decrees giving them unlimited power. They, combined with the VS, will win a majority at the next elections.

Russia is lost.

- @game_over: Game over.
